{
  "title": "51: al-Zaareyaat الذاريات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالذّٰرِيٰتِ ذَرْوًا ۙ‏(1)\n\nBy the scatterers that Scatter,\nفَالْحٰمِلٰتِ وِقْرًا ۙ‏(2)\n\nThen those which bear their load,\nفَالْجٰرِيٰتِ يُسْرًا ۙ‏(3)\n\nThen by those which speed lightly along,\nفَالْمُقَسِّمٰتِ اَمْرًا ۙ‏(4)\n\nThen by those distribute the affair,\nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَصَادِقٌ ۙ‏(5)\n\nVerily what ye are threatened with, is certainly true,\nوَّاِنَّ الدِّيْنَ لوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(6)\n\nAnd verily the Judgment shall surely come to pass.\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْحُبُكِ ۙ‏(7)\n\nAnd by the heaven with its starry highways,\nاِنَّكُمْ لَفِىْ قَوْلٍ مُّخْتَلِفٍ ۙ‏(8)\n\nVerily ye are in discordance in what ye say,\nيُّؤْفَكُ عَنْهُ مَنْ اُفِكَ ؕ‏(9)\n\nHe will be turned away from it who is to be turned away.\nقُتِلَ الْخَرّٰصُوْنَۙ‏(10)\n\nAccursed be the conjecturers,\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ سَاهُوْنَۙ‏(11)\n\nWho in the abyss (of ignorance) are wandering (bewildered),\nيَسْئَلُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(12)\n\nAsk they: “When is the Day of Judgment?\nيَوْمَ هُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ يُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(13)\n\nOn that day shall they be tried at the fire.\nذُوْقُوْا فِتْنَتَكُمْؕ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(14)\n\n(It will be said) “Taste ye (now) your trial (on the fire); This is what ye did seek to hasten on!\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(15)\n\nVerily the pious ones shall be in gardens and (among the) springs,\nاٰخِذِيْنَ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَبْلَ ذٰلِكَ مُحْسِنِيْنَؕ‏(16)\n\nReceiving (the enjoyment) what giveth them their Lord; Verily, they were ere that the doers of good.\nكَانُوْا قَلِيْلًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ مَا يَهْجَعُوْنَ‏(17)\n\nLittle of the night was it that they used to sleep.\nوَبِالْاَسْحَارِ هُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ‏(18)\n\nAnd in the (hours) ere the dawn they prayed for forgiveness.\nوَفِىْۤ اَمْوَالِهِمْ حَقٌّ لِّلسَّآئِلِ وَالْمَحْرُوْمِ‏(19)\n\nAnd in their property was a share due to the beggar and the destitute.\nوَفِى الْاَرْضِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّلْمُوْقِنِيْنَۙ‏(20)\n\nAnd in the earth are signs for those who are sure in faith,\nوَفِىْۤ اَنْفُسِكُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(21)\n\nAnd (also) in your own selves; will ye not then see?\nوَفِى السَّمَآءِ رِزْقُكُمْ وَمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(22)\n\nAnd in the heaven is your sustenance and what ye are promised with.\nفَوَرَبِّ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ مِّثْلَ مَاۤ اَنَّكُمْ تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(23)\n\nAnd by the Lord of the heavens and the earth! verily It (the Qur'an) is certainly the truth, just as ye speak,\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ ضَيْفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الْمُكْرَمِيْنَ‌ۘ‏(24)\n\nHas there come unto thee [O Muhammad] the story of Abraham’s honoured guests?\nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ ۚ قَوْمٌ مُّنْكَرُوْنَ‌‏(25)\n\nWhen entered they upon him said they: ‘Peace!’. ‘Peace! Said he [and deemed] A strange people [these are]\nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ فَجَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ سَمِيْنٍۙ‏(26)\n\nThen turned he aside unto his family, and brought a fat (roasted) calf\nفَقَرَّبَهٗۤ اِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(27)\n\nAnd set it near them. He said: ‘What! Eat ye not?\nفَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً‌ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ‌ ؕ وَبَشَّرُوْهُ بِغُلٰمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(28)\n\nAnd he conceived of them a fear; Said they: “Fear thou not!” and gave they the glad tidings unto him of a son blessed with knowledge\nفَاَقْبَلَتِ امْرَاَتُهٗ فِىْ صَرَّةٍ فَصَكَّتْ وَجْهَهَا وَقَالَتْ عَجُوْزٌ عَقِيْمٌ‏(29)\n\nThen came forward his wife in grief, she smote her face and said she (what! I) an old barren woman?\nقَالُوْا كَذٰلِكِ ۙ قَالَ رَبُّكِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(30)\n\nSaid they: “Thus sayeth thy Lord: ‘Verily He is the All-Wise, the All-Knowing\nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ اَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(31)\n\nHe said “What then is your errand, O’ ye Messengers?\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمٍ مُّجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(32)\n\nSaid they: ‘We are sent unto a criminal people\nلِنُرْسِلَ عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِّنْ طِيْنٍۙ‏(33)\n\nThat We may send down upon them stones of clay\nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لِلْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(34)\n\nMarked out from unto thy Lord for the guilty ones of excesses\nفَاَخْرَجْنَا مَنْ كَانَ فِيْهَا مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(35)\n\nAnd We brought forth (those) who were there in (the town) of the believers\nفَمَا وَجَدْنَا فِيْهَا غَيْرَ بَيْتٍ مِّنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(36)\n\nBut We found not there in (the town) save one house of the Muslims\nوَتَرَكْنَا فِيْهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَؕ‏(37)\n\nAnd left We therein a sign for those who dread the painful chastisement\nوَفِىْ مُوْسٰۤی اِذْ اَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\n\nAnd in Moses, when We sent him unto Pharaoh with manifest authority\nفَتَوَلّٰى بِرُكْنِهٖ وَقَالَ سٰحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‏(39)\n\nBut (Pharaoh) turned away with his forces and said (pointing to Moses): ‘(This is) a sorcerer or a madman\nفَاَخَذْنٰهُ وَجُنُوْدَهٗ فَنَبَذْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌؕ‏(40)\n\nSo, We seized him and his hosts and We cast them into the sea, for he was reprobate\nوَفِىْ عَادٍ اِذْ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّيْحَ الْعَقِيْمَ‌ۚ‏(41)\n\nAnd in ‘Ad: when sent We upon them the desolating (blast of violent’) wind\nمَا تَذَرُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ اَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ اِلَّا جَعَلَتْهُ كَالرَّمِيْمِؕ‏(42)\n\nIt left not aught upon which it came, but turned it like (rotten) dust\nوَفِىْ ثَمُوْدَ اِذْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَمَتَّعُوْا حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(43)\n\nAnd in Thamood: when it was said unto them; “Avail ye your- selves for a while\nفَعَتَوْا عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ وَ هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(44)\n\nBut rebelled they against the command of their Lord, so seized them the rumbling, while they were yet looking on\nفَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوْا مِنْ قِيَامٍ وَّمَا كَانُوْا مُنْتَصِرِيْنَۙ‏(45)\n\nThen they could not even rise (on their feet), nor could they help themselves\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(46)\n\nAnd the people of Noah before (that)’, Verily they were wicked people\nوَ السَّمَآءَ بَنَيْنٰهَا بِاَيْٮدٍ وَّاِنَّا لَمُوْسِعُوْنَ‏(47)\n\nAnd the heaven, We did raise it up with (Our) Might, and verily We are the expanders (of it) expanse?\nوَالْاَرْضَ فَرَشْنٰهَا فَنِعْمَ الْمٰهِدُوْنَ‏(48)\n\nAnd the earth, We did spread it out (like a carpet), how Excellent (are We) the Spreaders (thereof)?\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنَا زَوْجَيْنِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(49)\n\nAnd of everything have We created in pairs, that ye may reflect?\nفَفِرُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(50)\n\nSo fly ye unto God! Verily I am unto you a plain Warner\nوَلَا تَجْعَلُوْا مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(51)\n\nSet ye not with God any other god; Verily I am unto you a plain Warner\nكَذٰلِكَ مَاۤ اَتَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا قَالُوْا سَاحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‌ۚ‏(52)\n\nEven so there came not unto those before them an apostle but said they (of him): ‘A sorcerer or a mad man\nاَتَوَاصَوْا بِهٖ‌ۚ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\n\nHave they charged this unto one another? Nay! they are rebellious people\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمَلُوْمٍ‏(54)\n\nThen turn thou thy back upon them for thou art not to be blamed\nوَّذَكِّرْ فَاِنَّ الذِّكْرٰى تَنْفَعُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(55)\n\nAnd remind thou, for verily reminding profiteth the believers\nوَمَا خَلَقْتُ الْجِنَّ وَالْاِنْسَ اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْنِ‏(56)\n\nAnd created not I, the Jinn and the humans, but that they may worship (Me)\nمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ رِّزْقٍ وَّمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّطْعِمُوْنِ‏(57)\n\nI desire not from them any sustenance, nor do I desire that they should feed Me\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الرَّزَّاقُ ذُو الْقُوَّةِ الْمَتِيْنُ‏(58)\n\nVerily, God He (alone) is the Bestower of sustenance, the Lord of the unbreakable strength\nفَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذَنُوْبًا مِّثْلَ ذَنُوْبِ اَصْحٰبِهِمْ فَلَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنِ‏(59)\n\nSo, verily those who are unjust shall have a share (of the burden) like unto the share (of the burden) which had their fellows (of old), Therefore, let them ask Me not to hasten it on\nفَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ يَّوْمِهِمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(60)\n\nTherefore, Woe unto those who disbelieve because of their day which they are promised!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zaareyaat (The Scatterers)\nThere are 60 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of moving winds or breezes.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah increases ones sustenance and makes it easy to earn. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved after being written acts as a remedy for back problems (e.g. backaches). If a pregnant woman wears a talisman of Surah al-Zaareyaat, her pregnancy and delivery will be easy. Keeping this Surah close to a dying person makes his death easy."
